(6601748, 920931, 124815, '<td valign="top">So glad I stumbled upon this magnificent image and its story. You did a fantastic job with this picture.<br/>Well placed in the "Clouds" challenge. It''s totally amazing how different the clouds can be from one place to another. It''s as if they acquire the citizenship of each country. <br/>I love that you write the story of the shots. Thank you.</td>', 'So glad I stumbled upon this magnificent image and its story. You did a fantastic job with this picture.Well placed in the "Clouds" challenge. It''s totally amazing how different the clouds can be from one place to another. It''s as if they acquire the citizenship of each country. I love that you write the story of the shots. Thank you.', '2011-11-23 08:49:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6626428, 921198, 12611, '<td valign="top">This shot just hits all the right things about pretty barn sunsets. Excellent work.</td>', 'This shot just hits all the right things about pretty barn sunsets. Excellent work.', '2011-12-27 16:22:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6794200, 921507, 28710, '<td valign="top">It''s not the birds. It''s the motion they show.<br/> <br/>It''s not the motion of the birds. It''s the suggestion of motion, mirrored in the clouds.<br/> <br/>It''s not the suggestion of motion. It''s the feeling of being there. Sand in the toes. Salt in the nose. Wind in the hair. The dialogue between the crashing waves and the trickling of sand.<br/> <br/>It''s not the feeling of being there. It''s the hints of memories that are brought back of better times, healthier bodies, missed opportunities and bitter internal struggles fought alone on a backdrop of unforgiving, uncaring and untamed nature.<br/> <br/>It''s grey. And it''s great.</td>', 'It''s not the birds. It''s the motion they show. It''s not the motion of the birds. It''s the suggestion of motion, mirrored in the clouds. It''s not the suggestion of motion. It''s the feeling of being there. Sand in the toes. Salt in the nose. Wind in the hair. The dialogue between the crashing waves and the trickling of sand. It''s not the feeling of being there. It''s the hints of memories that are brought back of better times, healthier bodies, missed opportunities and bitter internal struggles fought alone on a backdrop of unforgiving, uncaring and untamed nature. It''s grey. And it''s great.', '2012-06-13 12:40:22.000000', NULL, 0),
